    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**. The build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Removed the `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` columns, their getters/setters, and the derived `getCheckDigit()`. Added a stored `member_id` column with `getMemberId()`/`setMemberId()`. Repointed `getPrimaryIdentifier()` to return the memberId.\n\n2. **`AssignMemberId.java`** (new, replacing `AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 Computes `memberId` = region + 2-digit fiscal year + 8 upper-hex SHA-256 of `telephone+lastName` + a Luhn CHK over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. Collision de-duplication now applies to the memberId (append `-<n>`). Deleted `AssignMembershipNumber.java`.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 Renamed the `customerCode` step to `memberId` (wired `AssignMemberId`, placed after registration-date defaulting so FY is available) and removed the `membershipNumber` step.\n\n4. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 The audit line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` JSON event now reference `memberId` (via `getPrimaryIdentifier()`) instead of the removed fields.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Swapped the ignore-mappings for the removed fields to `memberId`.\n\n6. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, and `membershipNumber` schema properties; added a `memberId` property (drives the generated DTO).\n\n7. **`schema.sql`** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 Renamed `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` and dropped `membership_number`.\n\nSample audit output confirms the format, e.g. `memberId=NSW271B92F1FC9` (NSW + FY 27 + HASH8 `1B92F1FC` + CHK `9`).",
